From: Etienne Cimon <etcimon@globecsys.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sifiveu: enable virtio-gpu DRM on QEMU virt

Add the in-kernel virtio-gpu DRM/KMS driver so the stock Linux driver
binds to QEMU's modern virtio-mmio GPU without a kmod package.

---
 target/linux/sifiveu/config-6.6 | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/sifiveu/config-6.6 b/target/linux/sifiveu/config-6.6
--- a/target/linux/sifiveu/config-6.6
+++ b/target/linux/sifiveu/config-6.6
@@ -424,7 +424,14 @@ CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO=y
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO_CMDLINE_DEVICES=y
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_CONSOLE=y
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_ANCHOR=y
+# Unchanged virtio-gpu DRM path. VIRTIO_GPU selects DRM_KMS_HELPER,
+# DRM_GEM_SHMEM_HELPER and VIRTIO_DMA_SHARED_BUFFER; olddefconfig resolves them.
+CONFIG_DRM=y
+CONFIG_DRM_VIRTIO_GPU=y
+CONFIG_DRM_VIRTIO_GPU_KMS=y
+CONFIG_FB=y
+CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_8250=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE=y
 CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_NR_UARTS=4
 CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_RUNTIME_UARTS=4
